li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Friday\">F<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Saturday\">S<\/abbr><\/li><\/ul> 9:35 AM  - 12:20 PM <\/td><td>G40 Kamphoefner Hall<\/td><td><a href=\"http:\/\/directory.ncsu.edu\/users\/azfarquh\" class=\"instructor-link\" target=\"_blank\">Farquharson,Ariana Zuri<\/a><\/td><td>08\/17\/26 - 12\/01\/26<\/td><td  class=\"hidden-xs\"><\/td><td  class=\"screen-only\"> <a href=\"#\" data-toggle=\"popover\" id=\"reqs-DS-100-002\"  data-placement\"left\" data-content=\"<p>R: 12DSBA<p>Departmental Approval Required\" data-title='Class Requisites: <button type=\"button\" class=\"popover-close close\">&times;<\/button>'><img src=\"images\/nc_yellow_diamond_warn.png\" alt=\"info icon\" title=\"more information available\" \/><\/a><a href='https:\/\/shop.ncsu.edu\/adoption-search' target='_blank'><img src='images\/books-icon.png' alt='View Books' title='View course books in Bookstore' \/><\/a><a href='syllabus.php?strm=2268&class_nbr=10309' target='_blank'><img src='images\/syllabus_file.png' alt='View Class Syllabus' title='View Class Syllabus' style='vertical-align:bottom;' \/><\/a><\/td>\n                                <\/tr><\/table><\/section> <!-- section DS-100 --><section class=\"course\" id=\"DS-200\"><h1>DS 200  <small>A Survey of Design Studies<\/small> <span class=\"units pull-right\">Units: 3<\/span><\/h1><p>This course will introduce students to a variety of perspectives and lenses through which to examine and evaluate design in the world. Students will consider design studies through theory and criticism of design, as well as applied to business administration, museum studies, and environmental studies. In addition, students will be encouraged to find evidence of and define design studies in areas that are uniquely suited to their individual areas of interest. As an advised elective, this course is required for Design Studies majors who are sophomores in their major.<\/p><p>Also listed as: ADN 200 <table class=\"table section-table table-striped table-condensed\" summary=\"This table details the sections of DS 200 based on the criteria submitted in the search form.\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sec<span class=\"hidden-xs\">tion<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\">Comp<span class=\"hidden-xs\">onent<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"class-num hidden-xs\">Class #<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Avail.<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Day\/Time<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Loc<span class=\"hidden-xs\">ation<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\">Instructor<\/th><th scope=\"col\"><span class=\"hidden-xs\">Begin\/End<\/span> Dates<\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"hidden-xs\">Topic<\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"screen-only\">Notes<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tfoot><tr><td colspan=\"6\"><a href=\"#container\">top<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tfoot><tr><td>001<\/td><td>Sem<\/td><td class=\"class-num hidden-xs\">6350<\/td><td><em><span class=\"text-danger\">Closed<\/span><\/em><br \/>0\/24<\/td><td><ul class=\"weekdisplay\"><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Sunday\">S<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"meet hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Monday - meet\">M<\/abbr><span class=\"screen-reader-only-text\"> meets<\/span><\/li><span class=\"visible-xs print-only\">M <\/span><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Tuesday\">T<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"meet hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Wednesday - meet\">W<\/abbr><span class=\"screen-reader-only-text\"> meets<\/span><\/li><span class=\"visible-xs print-only\">W <\/span><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Thursday\">T<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Friday\">F<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Saturday\">S<\/abbr><\/li><\/ul> 9:35 AM  - 11:25 AM <\/td><td>101 111 Lampe Drive<\/td><td><a href=\"http:\/\/directory.ncsu.edu\/users\/sewill32\" class=\"instructor-link\" target=\"_blank\">Williamson,Bess<\/a><\/td><td>08\/17\/26 - 12\/01\/26<\/td><td  class=\"hidden-xs\"><\/td><td  class=\"screen-only\"> <a href=\"#\" data-toggle=\"popover\" id=\"notes-DS-200-001\" data-content=\"This is a hybrid course section and will utilize both in-person and internet components. Your instructor will provide additional information regarding specific course requirements and when you should attend class in person.\" data-title='Class Notes: <button type=\"button\" class=\"popover-close close\">&times;<\/button>' data-placement=\"left\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-thin-menu\"><span class=\"screen-reader-only-text\">class notes<\/span><\/span><\/a> <a href=\"#\" data-toggle=\"popover\" id=\"reqs-DS-200-001\"  data-placement\"left\" data-content=\"<p>Prerequisite: D 100 and DS 100<p>Departmental Approval Required\" data-title='Class Requisites: <button type=\"button\" class=\"popover-close close\">&times;<\/button>'><img src=\"images\/nc_yellow_diamond_warn.png\" alt=\"info icon\" title=\"more information available\" \/><\/a><a href='https:\/\/shop.ncsu.edu\/adoption-search' target='_blank'><img src='images\/books-icon.png' alt='View Books' title='View course books in Bookstore' \/><\/a><a href='syllabus.php?strm=2268&class_nbr=6350' target='_blank'><img src='images\/syllabus_file.png' alt='View Class Syllabus' title='View Class Syllabus' style='vertical-align:bottom;' \/><\/a><\/td>\n                                <\/tr><\/table><\/section> <!-- section DS-200 --><section class=\"course\" id=\"DS-451\"><h1>DS 451  <small>Design Writing: Insight and Critique<\/small> <span class=\"units pull-right\">Units: 3<\/span><\/h1><p>This course will use writing to evaluate and critique contemporary design practice. Students will engage in a wide variety of writing forms, including personal essays, case study essays, critique and interviews. Students will also use visual thinking [concept mapping, illustration, visual essays] to explore methods of critical idea generation and to get more comfortable with the writing process. Students will be asked to compare and contrast how certain design theories are understood and applied within the different design disciplines [architecture, graphic design, industrial design, landscape architecture, fashion, fibers and new media] as well as in relation to science and humanity-based disciplines.<\/p><p>Prerequisites: ENG 101 and Sophomore Standing or above.<\/p><table class=\"table section-table table-striped table-condensed\" summary=\"This table details the sections of DS 451 based on the criteria submitted in the search form.\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sec<span class=\"hidden-xs\">tion<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\">Comp<span class=\"hidden-xs\">onent<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"class-num hidden-xs\">Class #<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Avail.<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Day\/Time<\/th><th scope=\"col\">Loc<span class=\"hidden-xs\">ation<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\">Instructor<\/th><th scope=\"col\"><span class=\"hidden-xs\">Begin\/End<\/span> Dates<\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"hidden-xs\">Topic<\/th><th scope=\"col\" class=\"screen-only\">Notes<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tfoot><tr><td colspan=\"6\"><a href=\"#container\">top<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tfoot><tr><td>001<\/td><td>Sem<\/td><td class=\"class-num hidden-xs\">10776<\/td><td><span class=\"text-success\">Open<\/span><br \/>9\/20<\/td><td><ul class=\"weekdisplay\"><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Sunday\">S<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"meet hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Monday - meet\">M<\/abbr><span class=\"screen-reader-only-text\"> meets<\/span><\/li><span class=\"visible-xs print-only\">M <\/span><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Tuesday\">T<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Wednesday\">W<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Thursday\">T<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Friday\">F<\/abbr><\/li><li class=\"open hidden-xs\"><abbr title=\"Saturday\">S<\/abbr><\/li><\/ul> 1:30 PM  - 4:15 PM <\/td><td>312 Leazar Hall<\/td><td><a href=\"http:\/\/directory.ncsu.edu\/users\/jsgant\" class=\"instructor-link\" target=\"_blank\">Gant,Jedidiah<\/a><\/td><td>08\/17\/26 - 12\/01\/26<\/td><td  class=\"hidden-xs\"><\/td><td  class=\"screen-only\"> <a href=\"#\" data-toggle=\"popover\" id=\"reqs-DS-451-001\"  data-placement\"left\" data-content=\"<p>Departmental Approval Required\" data-title='Class Requisites: <button type=\"button\" class=\"popover-close close\">&times;<\/button>'><img src=\"images\/nc_yellow_diamond_warn.png\" alt=\"info icon\" title=\"more information available\" \/><\/a><a href='https:\/\/shop.ncsu.edu\/adoption-search' target='_blank'><img src='images\/books-icon.png' alt='View Books' title='View course books in Bookstore' \/><\/a><a href='syllabus.php?strm=2268&class_nbr=10776' target='_blank'><img src='images\/syllabus_file.png' alt='View Class Syllabus' title='View Class Syllabus' style='vertical-align:bottom;' \/><\/a><\/td>\n                                <\/tr><\/table><\/section> <!-- section DS-451 --><section class=\"course\" id=\"DS-481\"><h1>DS 481  <small>Design Studies Senior Research Seminar<\/small> <span class=\"units pull-right\">Units: 3<\/span><\/h1><p>Each student in Design Studies will develop a topic for his or her Senior Capstone Research Paper to be done during the Spring term. During the Research semester, each student will develop a comprehensive bibliography for the topic and an outline ofthe paper. One paper will be written before the end of the term that addresses issues directly related to the Capstone Research paper. Throughout the term, students will share their research with others in the seminar.<\/p><p>Prerequisite: Completion of all course work in DS through junior year ; Design Studies Majors<\/p><table class=\"table section-table table-striped table-condensed\" summary=\"This table details the sections of DS 481 based on the criteria submitted in the search form.\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sec<span class=\"hidden-xs\">tion<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\">Comp<span class=\"hidden-xs\">onent<\/span><\/th><th scope=\"col\" class